Differentiating $I_D$ w.r.t. $V_D$, we get

\begin{gathered}
\frac{d}{d V_D}\left(I_D\right)=\frac{d}{d V_D}\left(7.8 \times 10^{-5} e^{6.9 V_D}\right) \\
=7.8 \times 10^{-5} \times 6.9 \times e^{6.9 V_D} \\
=I_D \times 6.9
\end{gathered}

Dynamic resistance is $\frac{d}{d I_D}\left(V_D\right)$
\Rightarrow \quad \frac{d V_D}{d I_D}=\frac{1}{6.9 \times I_D}

When $I_D=4 \mathrm{~mA}=4 \times 10^{-3} \mathrm{~A}$
Then,

\begin{aligned}
\frac{d V_D}{d I_D} & =\frac{1}{6.9 \times 4 \times 10^{-3}} \\
& =36.23 \Omega
\end{aligned}

$\therefore$ Dynamic resistance $=36.23 \Omega$

